WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.420
Do you have some questions about the upcoming
Hellboy film?

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.420
Questions like: why film a reboot at all?

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:06.420
Why is it R-rated?

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.560
Or, if you're new to this whole scene, perhaps
you're just wondering who Hellboy is in the

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.500
first place?

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:12.940
Well, we're here to help.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.860
Hellboy was originally conceived in 1991 by
comic creator Mike Mignola, and appeared in

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.360
various one-off stories and illustrations
before his own title arrived in 1994.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.480
Despite his bright red, horned humanoid appearance,
Hellboy is technically only half-demon, as

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.660
the comics establish him to be the child of
a Duke of Hell and a human witch.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.980
Born in Hell after his mother's body was taken
there by his biological father, Hellboy was

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:44.870
summoned to Earth in 1944 as the result of
a Nazi occult ritual led by the sorcerer Grigori

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:50.180
Rasputin . In the comics, he appears in England,
where American soldiers and Professor Trevor

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:52.120
Bruttenholm are investigating Nazi activity.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.620
"But nevertheless, a name we all came to use.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.280
We called him: Hellboy."

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:05.700
Over time, it became clear that the young
Hellboy was, despite his appearance, an apparently

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:10.240
good soul, and in a matter of years he was
recruited to become the world's most effective

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.520
paranormal investigator.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.060
Working with Bruttenholm as his mentor and
surrogate father, Hellboy travels the world

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.000
battling various paranormal threats.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.600
As a half-demon, Hellboy possesses extraordinary
strength and durability that allow him to

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.280
continue fighting well past human limits.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.160
Perhaps most importantly, he's basically fireproof,
which makes sense for someone who's half Hellspawn.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.500
Then there's the matter of his right hand.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:42.200
"And I beheld an angel, and in his right hand,
was the key to the bottomless pit."

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.880
Known as the Right Hand of Doom, it was grafted
onto his infant body by his father at birth.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.740
The hand originally belonged to an ancient
spirit called Anum, who was the creator of

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:56.829
the Ogdru Jahad, legendary imprisoned creatures
who are prophesied to one day be released

00:01:56.829 --> 00:01:58.360
and bring about the end of the world.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.590
Hellboy's Right Hand is the key to releasing
and controlling the Ogdru Jahad, even if Hellboy

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.920
himself would rather not.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:09.180
Beyond that, it's also a big heavy hand that
he can use to hit monsters with.

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:13.840
In more recent comic book stories, Hellboy
has assumed greater control over his demonic

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:18.050
form, to the point that he can manipulate
his own size and even sprout wings and full

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:22.900
horns when he wishes, although this is not
generally an ability explored in film versions

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.320
of the character... yet.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.600
In the 2019 Hellboy, Milla Jovovich plays
Nimue.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.940
Originally known as the Lady of the Lake,
Nimue is a being from Arthurian legend that

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.260
was a powerful witch, and extremely close
to Merlin.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.860
Merlin told her all of his magical secrets,
but she ultimately imprisoned him and went

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.060
mad with the dark knowledge.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.220
She was eventually killed when all the other
witches of Britain banded together to kill

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.440
her and seal her body deep in a tomb.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.620
In the comic story The Wild Hunt, Nimue is
resurrected after she's nominated to become

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.140
the leader of the witches of Britain, many
of whom flee in terror from her power.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.620
It's during this storyline that Morgana le
Fay reveals to Hellboy that he's actually

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:05.880
the last heir of King Arthur, setting up a
showdown between Hellboy and Nimue that could

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.900
bring about the end of the world.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.120
Suffice it to say, Nimue is bad news indeed.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:16.030
Hellboy wouldn't be who he is without Professor
Trevor Bruttenholm, the man who found and

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:19.460
essentially adopted him in 1944 when he first
appeared on Earth.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:24.240
Bruttenholm is an English occult expert who
began working with Allied forces in World

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:28.440
War II when it became clear that the Nazis
were planning to call demonic forces to earth.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.700
After the war, Broom helped to form the Bureau
for Paranormal Research and Defense, and he

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.500
and Hellboy battled various occult threats
together until Broom's retirement as director

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.140
of the agency.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:44.680
In the comics, Broom was killed in 1994 by
a frog monster tied to the Ogdru Jahad, and

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:48.320
had a similarly gruesome end in 2004's Hellboy
movie.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:53.480
He was played by John Hurt in both the original
and 2008's Hellboy II: The Golden Army, and

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.120
is played by Ian McShane in the 2019 film.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:01.900
Throughout his comic book and cinematic history,
Hellboy has retained close ties to the Bureau

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.000
for Paranormal Research and Defense, or B.P.R.D.

00:04:05.629 --> 00:04:08.180
The bureau's mission statement is right there
in its name.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:12.420
"There are things that go bump in the night,
Agent Myers, make no mistake about that.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.320
We are the things that go bump back."

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.950
Its job is to research and combat various
occult threats and phenomena that may pose

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:25.600
a threat to humanity, often with the aid of
various supernatural entities and humans who

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.220
have been gifted with special abilities.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:32.500
Hellboy is the most prominent of these members,
but the bureau has also included members like

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.760
the fish man Abe Sapien, and the pyrokinetic
human Elizabeth Sherman.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:43.060
In the 2019 film, the B.P.R.D. also includes
Ben Daimio, a B.P.R.D. agent who was killed

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.880
by a jaguar cult on assignment in Bolivia.

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:51.840
Daimio rose from the dead, and has since manifested
the ability to transform into a jaguar creature.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:56.580
In November of 2018, a last-minute casting
addition was announced for the new Hellboy

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:02.000
film: Thomas Haden Church joined the reboot
as Lobster Johnson, a character created by

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:07.760
Mike Mignola in 1999 as an homage to various
pulp heroes of the early twentieth-century.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.500
In the comics, "The Lobster" was a vigilante
in Depression-era New York City, known for

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.350
burning his lobster emblem into the flesh
of criminals.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:19.740
To the public, he was thought to be an urban
legend, and eventually a fictional character

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:20.860
dreamed up by a pulp writer.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.080
Instead, the Lobster was real enough to begin
working for the U.S. government in the late

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.040
1930s in an effort to thwart various Nazi
missions.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:34.600
He died in 1939 while attempting to stop a
Nazi space launch that would have possibly

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.500
put the Third Reich into space.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:41.860
In 2001, he appeared in the Conqueror Worm
storyline as a ghost who haunts the ruins

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.160
of the castle where he died.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:47.820
He's made occasional appearances in the comics
since, lending a ghostly helping hand to the

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.780
B.P.R.D. against supernatural threats.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:55.500
The first two Hellboy films were masterminded
by director Guillermo del Toro, with Ron Perlman

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.020
in the title role.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:00.740
Hellboy II: The Golden Army ends with a hint
for more Hellboy story to come.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:05.800
Unfortunately, the film underperformed, and
a planned third movie didn't materialize.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:11.840
As years went by, del Toro continued to express
interest, but in early 2017 he announced that

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.760
all efforts had finally been exhausted.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:17.640
Months later, the reboot was announced without
del Toro attached.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:22.260
According to Hellboy creator Mike Mignola,
there was some talk of trying to continue

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:26.740
del Toro's story with a new film, but he felt
that wouldn't be fair to a new team of filmmakers.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.440
He told SyFy that he was looking forward to
director Neil Marshal's take:

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:36.040
In the summer of 2017, the Hellboy reboot
ignited an uproar with a casting announcement.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:39.140
Ed Skrein was confirmed to play Ben Daimio.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:44.540
In the comics, Daimio is Japanese-American,
and this heritage plays a major role in both

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.160
his life and in the B.P.R.D. comics stories.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.160
Fans were confused and upset that the production
didn't cast a Japanese-American actor to better

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:53.700
depict the character on-screen.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:58.220
Skrein became aware of the outcry after taking
the roll, and released a statement saying

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:00.880
he would be departing the production to make
room for another actor.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:07.360
Then, in September 2017, Korean-American actor
Daniel Dae Kim signed on to play the role

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:07.960
of Ben Daimio.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:12.610
Thanks to the cast and crew's willingness
to correct themselves, we got a Ben Daimio

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:16.320
who looks more like the Ben that fans were
introduced to on the comics page.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:22.010
Both of Hellboy's previous big-screen adventures
were PG-13 rated fantasy adventures with certain

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:22.760
horror elements.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.360
However, in 2017, Hellboy director Neil Marshall
remarked that he had been granted permission

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:33.070
to take the film into R-rated territory, which
he saw not as a mandate, but as a license

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:36.160
to depict the same level of violence often
explored in the comics.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:42.240
In February of 2019, the Hellboy reboot was
officially rated R for "strong bloody violence

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.280
and gore throughout."

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.500
It also earned that rating because of language.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.360
Star David Harbour explained to MTV :

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:53.260
"It goes R for a bit of gore and horror, but
also a bit of just the mature aspect of it,

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:54.100
the mature themes of it.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.260
Just that we’re dealing with complicated
subjects."

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:02.380
The first Hellboy film was a loose adaptation
of his first major story, Seed of Destruction.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:07.220
The sequel, The Golden Army, was an original
story conceived by Guillermo del Toro, and

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.000
the third film would have followed that concept.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.360
For the reboot, Mignola and company didn't
necessarily want to retell the character's

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.820
origin story, but they did want to draw heavily
from the original comics.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:22.720
That means that much of Hellboy 2019 will
come from various Hellboy comics.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:28.300
The Wild Hunt, Darkness Calls, The Storm and
the Fury, and Hellboy in Mexico are just some

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.800
of the storylines that have been clearly referenced
in trailers and interview junkets.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:36.870
In terms of the look of the film, concept
artists pulled direct inspiration from comics

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:41.000
by Mignola and other artists, then adapted
them to a more real-world look.

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.750
Makeup artist Joel Harlow told SyFy:

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:47.900
"What we wanted to do with the character was
to make him feel grittier, to feel not so

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:51.160
much like a comic character what would this
character look like if he was in the real

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:51.700
world?

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.540
Hence the addition of the scars and the addition
of the hair and the overall sort of weathering

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.520
on him that you do find in the illustrations."

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:03.320
David Harbour became a star in the eyes of
genre fans thanks to his role as Chief Hopper

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:07.570
in Stranger Things, a role that gave him the
prominence necessary to get a blockbuster

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:08.340
job like Hellboy.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:13.300
Playing Hellboy created a different set of
challenges for Harbour, though, and not just

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.000
because of the prosthetic applications and
all the stunt work.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:20.700
Playing Hellboy also meant stepping into a
role already made famous by Ron Perlman.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.000
So how did Harbour decide to take the job?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.940
By finding a new approach to the source material.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:29.920
Harbour told The Hollywood Reporter that he
struggled with whether or not to do the film:

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:35.040
"I'm a fan of those movies, and Guillermo
is obviously an extraordinary director and

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.480
Ron’s an extraordinary actor, and his definition
of that role was very iconic.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.050
So in terms of approaching it, even when they
approached me I was like, 'why do it?

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:44.000
It’s already been done.'

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.260
And they said they wanted to do it differently.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:51.000
And there is something when you go back to
the actual graphic novel that is a bit darker

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:51.800
and bit less clean.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:56.640
And even in terms of the character arc of
Hellboy himself, this piece focuses a little

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:57.960
more on his internal struggles.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.040
I equate it to Hamlet, a little bit, it’s
got a certain Hamlet feel to it."

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:05.540
Presumably, there's a little more action in
this version of Hamlet.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:09.200
"To be or not to be…

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:11.820
Not to be."

